Upstream attribution

This project adapts and extends work from the Comfy-Org ecosystem:

* The asym_w4a8_int8 ("W4A8") quantization scheme, its ConvRot layout, and
  the codebook/scale tensor contracts follow comfy-kitchen PR #90
  (commit aa1ab2263dc06225d9de6702dfc087313d4bc971) and ComfyUI PR #15308
  (head 8c3a2b27c37bd34e87b58846baf962407c92843c).
* The int8_tensorwise rowwise scheme matches the Comfy-Org int8_convrot
  checkpoint family (without ConvRot).
* The convrot_w4a4 layout and the W4A4/W4A8/INT8 eager kernels used by the
  companion tools (tools/runtime_certify.py, testdata/runtime_equivalence.py,
  testdata/cuda_smoke.py) are implemented in comfy-kitchen
  (https://github.com/Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen), Copyright (c) Comfy Org,
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The standalone converter (comfyui_wxa8_quantizer.py) is original code that
emits payloads conforming to those upstream contracts; it does not import or
vendor comfy-kitchen code at runtime. Where upstream code or contracts were
adapted, the Apache-2.0 license terms of the respective upstream projects
apply to the adapted portions.
